WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:09.000
Tuesday, 7:40. Laras opens her inbox before work.

2
00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:15.500
Rejection number nine. This time she failed an online test at stage two.

3
00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:20.800
At nine, her team lead has news for the interns.

4
00:00:20.800 --> 00:00:29.700
The reporting tool she spent a month learning is gone. From today, the team works in a new one.

5
00:00:29.700 --> 00:00:36.200
Two bad surprises in one morning. But they are not the same problem.

6
00:00:36.200 --> 00:00:42.300
The new tool asks Laras to change her method. That is adaptability.

7
00:00:42.300 --> 00:00:47.600
The rejection drains her energy. Getting it back is resilience.

8
00:00:47.600 --> 00:00:55.300
You can be strong in one and weak in the other. And both can be trained.

9
00:00:55.300 --> 00:01:03.000
For the rejection, Laras runs a recovery loop. It has four steps and takes fifteen minutes.

10
00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:11.500
Name it, precisely. Not “I am bad at this”, but “I failed the numerical test at stage two.”

11
00:01:11.500 --> 00:01:20.400
Normalise it. Most applicants are rejected most of the time. This is the terrain, not a verdict on her.

12
00:01:20.400 --> 00:01:27.700
Extract one thing she controls. She ran out of time on the last ten questions.

13
00:01:27.700 --> 00:01:36.200
Choose the next step, and put it in the calendar. Twenty minutes of timed practice, tomorrow at eight.

14
00:01:36.200 --> 00:01:41.100
Wednesday, eight o'clock. A timer, twenty minutes, ten questions.

15
00:01:41.100 --> 00:01:46.400
She still gets two wrong. But this time she finishes.

16
00:01:46.400 --> 00:01:52.500
For the new tool, the answer is different. She changes her method.

17
00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:59.400
She asks a teammate for fifteen minutes, then rebuilds one small report by herself.

18
00:01:59.400 --> 00:02:04.700
Friday. Laras presents her first report in the new tool.

19
00:02:04.700 --> 00:02:11.200
Nobody calls it the new tool any more. It is just the tool.

20
00:02:11.200 --> 00:02:14.900
A setback you process becomes data.

21
00:02:14.900 --> 00:02:18.600
A setback you avoid becomes fear.

22
00:02:18.600 --> 00:02:22.300
Adaptability is a decision about method.

23
00:02:22.300 --> 00:02:26.000
Resilience is a discipline about energy.

24
00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:33.700
Now it is your turn. Pick one setback from the last month, and run the loop.
